symbols.documentation:
Construct terminal biology and virgin per-recruit biomass, and average the requested historical fishing-pattern years.
@param d Borrowed validated input schema; must outlive the benchmark calculator.
@param values Borrowed native parameter map, including fixed biology; must outlive this object.
@param deviations Historical fitted log recruitment deviations, including early age-structure effects.
@param first_pattern_year First historical year averaged into the fishing pattern; zero means terminal year.
@param last_pattern_year Last historical year averaged into the fishing pattern; zero means terminal year.
@details data and values are borrowed; do not destroy or modify them while using this calculator. Zero reference-year arguments select the terminal year.

Solve positive Beverton-Holt recruitment, equilibrium abundance, yield and SS3 units-4 annual F for a nonnegative fishing multiplier.
@param scale Nonnegative common multiplier on the reference apical-rate pattern.
@return Equilibrium summaries; recruitment is clamped to zero beyond the positive BH equilibrium.

Use bracket expansion and bisection to find a valid fractional SPR or virgin-biomass target.
@param value Target fraction in (0,1), interpreted by spawning_ratio.
@param spawning_ratio True targets equilibrium SSB divided by unfished SSB; false targets raw SPR.
@return Equilibrium summaries at the bracketed target fishing multiplier.

Find maximum equilibrium yield through a bracketed fourth-order numerical derivative root, avoiding flat-objective rounding noise.
@return Equilibrium summaries at the yield-derivative root.
@details The five-point numerical yield derivative avoids comparing almost equal maxima. Its fixed step and bracket tolerance are checked indirectly by the two-step forecast uncertainty validation; this is not a global optimizer for arbitrary selectivity models.

Populate a parameter map from control initial values; these may differ from fitted Report.sso values.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Parsed controls whose initial native values are read; report-fitted values are separate fixtures.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Calculate a numerically stable inverse-logit for ordinary or AD scalars.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Unconstrained scalar log-odds; evaluated with a value-based stable branch.
@return Inverse-logit probability on the same scalar/AD tape as x.

Approximate the standard normal CDF with scalar-generic operations, enabling differentiation through age-length probabilities.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Standard-normal deviate; derivatives follow the smooth approximation.
@return Approximate normal cumulative probability on the same scalar/AD tape as x.

Integrate normal lengths across lower-edge bins, accumulating the two tails in the end bins and rejecting invalid grids or scale.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param edges Strictly increasing lower length-bin edges in cm; end bins accumulate the tails.
@param mean Mean individual length in cm.
@param sd Strictly positive length standard deviation in cm.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Calculate sex-specific mean length with the supplied birth timing, seasonal growth and SS3 plus-group growth adjustment.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@param year_fraction Time within the calendar year in years; not the fraction of the current season.
@return Mean length in cm, including the supported plus-group adjustment.

Interpolate age-dependent length variability and convert its coefficient of variation to a standard deviation.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@param time Within-year time passed through to the mean-length calculation.
@param mean Mean individual length in cm.
@return Length standard deviation in cm.

Return bin probabilities for one sex, age and within-year time using fitted growth parameters.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@param time Within-year time in years at which growth/length integration is evaluated.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Map a population length-bin lower edge to its integration midpoint, including the final bin convention.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param bin Zero-based index into the population length integration grid.
@return Integration midpoint in cm.

Evaluate the sex-specific length-weight power relationship; length is cm and individual weight is kg.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param length Individual length in cm.
@return Individual weight in kg.

Evaluate the length-based logistic female maturity curve from its midpoint and slope.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param length Individual length in cm.
@return Mature fraction at the supplied length.

Integrate individual weight over the age-length key at a supplied within-year time.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@param time Within-year time in years at which growth/length integration is evaluated.
@return Mean individual weight in kg.

Locate the start of the subseason containing spawning, matching the supplied SS3 maturity integration convention.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Integrate mature female biomass contribution across length bins, respecting the first mature age.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
