Read one CSV record, accepting LF/CRLF and reporting stream exhaustion.
@param in Input stream; record extraction advances its position.
@param line One unquoted CSV record (or output record buffer for csv_line).
@return True for an extracted record; false only when no next line can be extracted.

Split the deliberately unquoted, single-line CSV schema; retain empty fields.
@param line One unquoted CSV record (or output record buffer for csv_line).
@return All fields in order, including a final empty field after a trailing comma.

Parse an entire decimal integer token; reject suffixes, overflow and blanks.
@param text Entire numeric token; partial parses and coercion are not accepted.
@return Exactly parsed decimal integer.

Parse an entire finite floating-point token, rejecting range errors and whitespace.
@param text Entire numeric token; partial parses and coercion are not accepted.
@return Exactly parsed finite decimal floating-point value.

Construct an explicitly zero-filled sex-by-age state, including AD scalars whose default constructor does not initialize a numerical zero.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@return A new state containing numerical T(0) in every cell.

Map zero-based sex and age to the flattened 32-cell population-state index; callers supply sex 0-1 and age 0-15.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@return Sex-major offset sex*nage+age; no bounds check is performed by this primitive.

Propagate a compatible finite output Jacobian through the full parameter covariance as J V J-transpose, preserving correlations.
@param jacobian Output-by-coordinate derivative matrix, with columns in the covariance coordinate order.
@param covariance Square, finite, symmetric positive-definite covariance of independent fitting coordinates.
@return Native output covariance J*V*J-transpose, which may be rank deficient.
@details Columns of jacobian must correspond exactly to covariance rows. Keeping only marginal parameter variances would omit compensating/correlated effects and change the reported uncertainties.

Construct a pointwise positive 95% interval from a positive estimate and nonnegative native variance; reject nonfinite results.
@param estimate Strictly positive native-scale output estimate.
@param variance Nonnegative finite native-scale marginal variance, not a standard deviation.
@return Native SE and positive pointwise 95% log-scale Wald bounds.
@details Bounds are estimate*exp(+-1.95996398454005*SE/estimate). They are not bootstrap quantiles, simultaneous trajectory bands or intervals for realized future recruitment.

Calculate the stable Baranov exposure (1-exp(-Z*duration))/Z, using a near-zero expansion; Z is an annual rate and duration is years.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param z Total annual instantaneous mortality; callers supply nonnegative rates.
@param duration Exposure duration in calendar years; a quarter is 0.25.
@return Integrated survival per unit abundance; its limit as z tends to zero is duration.

Apply natural and fleet fishing mortality over a fraction of a year, returning survivors and separately attributed removals without altering the input state.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param m Fixed sex-by-age natural mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param fleet_f Per-fleet sex-by-age fishing mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param duration Exposure duration in calendar years; a quarter is 0.25.
@return Survivors, natural deaths and fleet catch numbers on the input abundance scale.

Advance survivors one age at the calendar-year boundary, retain accumulated ages in the plus group and clear age zero.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param survivors Post-mortality abundance in thousands of fish, before January aging.
@return A new January state, retaining old plus-group survivors and admitting age-14 survivors.

Mutate age-zero abundance by adding recruitment allocated to females and males using the supplied female fraction.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param recruits Recruitment in thousands of fish to allocate at the July settlement event.
@param female_fraction Recruitment fraction assigned to females; male allocation is its complement.
@post Only age-zero cells are incremented; other ages and caller parameter values are unchanged.

Calculate female mature biomass after survival to a calendar-correct within-season spawning time.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param m Fixed sex-by-age natural mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param fleet_f Per-fleet sex-by-age fishing mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param mature_weight Mature female weight contribution per fish in kg, indexed by age.
@param elapsed Calendar-year fraction between seasonal beginning and spawning.
@return Female spawning biomass in tonnes under calendar-correct survival.

Reproduce the legacy SS3 v3.30.20 spawning-survival timing convention used by the supplied benchmark, deliberately distinct from the calendar-correct helper.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param m Fixed sex-by-age natural mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param fleet_f Per-fleet sex-by-age fishing mortality, expressed as annual instantaneous rates.
@param mature_weight Mature female weight contribution per fish in kg, indexed by age.
@param calendar_elapsed Calendar-year fraction from seasonal beginning to spawning.
@param season_duration Season length in years; used to reconstruct the legacy SS3 within-season fraction.
@return Female spawning biomass in tonnes under legacy v3.30.20 survival.
@warning calendar_elapsed/season_duration is used directly against annual mortality to reproduce this SS3 version. For May spawning in Q2, this is 1/3 rather than 1/12 calendar years; use the separate calendar helper for that alternative definition.

Evaluate the ordinary von Bertalanffy growth curve at a real age using fixed growth settings and length at birth.
@param real_age Elapsed years since birth, including fractional age.
@param g Fixed growth reference ages, lengths, rate and variability for one sex.
@param length_at_birth Mean length at birth in cm.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Return expected recruitment from spawning biomass, virgin recruitment, virgin spawning biomass and steepness; retain scalar-generic derivatives.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param ssb Female spawning biomass in tonnes under the specified timing convention.
@param r0 Virgin expected annual recruitment in thousands of fish.
@param b0 Virgin spawning biomass in tonnes, consistent with r0.
@param h Beverton-Holt steepness on its native scale.
@return Expected recruitment in thousands of fish; no stochastic deviation is drawn.

Resolve a component/fleet likelihood lambda at the requested estimation phase.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param component SS3 likelihood-component code, as stored in lambda_changes.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector offset.
@param phase Estimation phase used to resolve persistent lambda changes.
@return Effective lambda after applicable changes persist through the selected phase.

Apply a parsed variance adjustment for an observation kind and fleet to its initial error value.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param kind SS3 variance-adjustment kind code.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector offset.
@param initial Default adjustment/error value when no matching control row exists.
@return Configured replacement value or initial when no row matches.

Return a checked reference to one historical year-season row; reject missing or out-of-range calendar positions.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param run Completed historical population trajectory; references into it must not outlive it.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active control blocks.
@param season One-based quarter, 1..4.
@return Borrowed reference into run; destruction/mutation of run invalidates the reference.

Translate a source observation month and fleet timing setting into the season and exposure times used for index and composition prediction.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector offset.
@param month Source observation month, in [1,13); fractional months retain their supplied timing.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Project selected surviving numbers into sex-specific sampled length frequencies for an observation time.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param row One historical population-season row with beginning numbers and fitted fishing rates.
@param curve One fleet length-selectivity vector on the population integration grid.
@param time Resolved observation timing; negative elapsed selects the supported season-integrated convention.
@param cached Optional age-length keys from this same parameter evaluation and time; nullptr recomputes them.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Analytically profile log catchability as an inverse-variance-weighted log residual mean, using the exact source stabilization.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param log_base Log model predictions before catchability, already using the required stabilizer.
@param observed Strictly positive index observations aligned with log_base.
@param se Positive log-scale standard errors; inverse squared values define the profiling weights.
@param use Inclusion flags aligned with observations and error vectors.
@param bias_adjust Whether to apply the supported lognormal catchability bias correction.
@return Analytical optimum log catchability; zero when no included observations exist.

Evaluate the index lognormal negative log-likelihood under the configured standard-deviation offset convention.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param log_expected Expected observation on the natural-log scale.
@param observed Strictly positive index observation on its native scale.
@param se Positive log-scale standard error for this observation.
@param sd_offset Configured multiplier of the log-standard-error term in the likelihood.
@return Unweighted lognormal contribution, including the configured SD offset.

Calculate sample-size-weighted multinomial composition deviance against a perfect-fit offset after probability stabilization.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param observed Observed length-bin proportions after the supported stabilization/normalization.
@param expected Strictly positive expected bin proportions aligned with observed.
@param n Positive effective sample size after the supplied composition weighting.
@return Unweighted multinomial perfect-fit-offset deviance.

Evaluate SS3's stabilized log catch residual penalty for observed and predicted fleet-unit catch.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param observed Strictly positive fleet-unit observed catch.
@param predicted Predicted catch in the same fleet units as observed.
@param se Positive log-scale catch standard error.
@return Unweighted stabilized log catch residual penalty.

Evaluate the supported symmetric-beta soft-bound penalty on estimated selectivity parameters.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Sum squared historical log recruitment deviations and the bias-weighted log-sigma contribution for the joint likelihood target.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param dev Year-to-log-recruitment-deviation map; the caller enforces the main-period constraint.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Calculate catch, index, length-composition, recruitment and soft-bound components from a population trajectory; preserve all configured lambdas.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param deviations Historical fitted log recruitment deviations, including early age-structure effects.
@param run Completed historical population trajectory; references into it must not outlive it.
@param phase Estimation phase used to resolve persistent lambda changes.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Build the fitting-coordinate schema from estimated control parameters and independent early/main recruitment deviations.
@param input Input schema transferred into the owning model adapter.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param deviations Historical fitted log recruitment deviations, including early age-structure effects.

Transform fitting coordinates to native parameters/deviations and enforce the zero-sum main-deviation constraint, including the dependent final year.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Independent bounded-logit coordinates in free/parameter_names_impl order; length must match free.size().
@return Native parameter/deviation maps; the final main deviation is dependent.
@details For main years before the final year, deviations are independent bounded coordinates. The final value is minus their sum, so its box bound must be checked separately. No logit Jacobian is added to an MLE objective.
@throws std::invalid_argument On a coordinate count mismatch or an infeasible dependent final deviation.

Decode coordinates, run the population and return the complete component-wise likelihood result.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Independent bounded-logit coordinates in free/parameter_names_impl order; length must match free.size().
@return Population-derived components, fits and total joint objective.

Return only the joint scalar objective for a supplied fitting-coordinate vector.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Independent bounded-logit coordinates in free/parameter_names_impl order; length must match free.size().
@return Joint penalized negative log-likelihood; no Laplace or transform-density term.

Evaluate the scalar objective through Quadra's model interface and register it in the report context.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param x Independent bounded-logit coordinates in free/parameter_names_impl order; length must match free.size().
@param context Quadra report context receiving objective diagnostics.
@return Joint objective, also registered in context.

Integrate growth, selectivity and mature weight for one of four seasons; produce all fleet/sex/age factors needed by population dynamics.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param curves Fleet length-selectivity vectors for the chosen year/block combination.
@param season One-based quarter, 1..4.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Multiply fleet apical annual fishing rates by numbers selectivity to obtain fleet-specific sex/age mortality arrays.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param apical Annual apical fishing rates, indexed by season and fleet where applicable.
@param b Seasonal selection/weight integration consistent with the rate vectors.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Reproduce SS3 method-3 finite catch tuning, including Pope initialization, smooth caps, mixed catch units and the configured finite adjustment count.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param biology Seasonal selection, weight and maturity factors from the same native parameters.
@param observed Fleet catches in their configured units: tonnes or thousands of fish; zero means no observed catch.
@param duration Exposure duration in calendar years; a quarter is 0.25.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Evaluate the piecewise recruitment-bias ramp for a historical year from the advanced control settings.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active control blocks.
@return Configured bias-ramp fraction for the year.

Apply a year's fitted deviation and log-bias correction to expected recruitment without changing the deviation map.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param dev Year-to-log-recruitment-deviation map; the caller enforces the main-period constraint.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active control blocks.
@param expected Beverton-Holt expected recruitment in thousands of fish, before deviation/bias adjustment.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Combine beginning numbers, fishing mortality and mature weights to compute spawning biomass under SS3 v3.30.20 timing.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param numbers Sex-by-age abundance at the start of the calculation, in thousands of fish.
@param fishing Fleet-specific sex-by-age fishing mortality arrays in annual rate units.
@param biology Seasonal selection, weight and maturity factors from the same native parameters.
@param season One-based quarter, 1..4.
@return Female spawning biomass in tonnes, using legacy SS3 timing.

Solve the stationary seasonal sex/age population for supplied fishing rates and recruitment, including July settlement and the plus group.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and estimated values must be present.
@param biology Seasonal selection, weight and maturity factors from the same native parameters.
@param apical Annual apical fishing rates, indexed by season and fleet where applicable.
@param recruitment Constant equilibrium recruitment in thousands of fish.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing conventions.

Calculate virgin and initial-fishing Beverton-Holt equilibria, then apply early deviations and bias correction to the initial age structure.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active evaluation tape.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish assessment.
